# G123 — Screen Capture Program

*v2. See `screen-capture.md` for prose: region ADT, delay FSM with countdown,
annotation overlays distinct from transforms, Bresenham lines, window lookup
injected at capture time.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Screenshot Workflow

[screenshot-workflow
    IN ORDER TO
        capture screen regions on hotkey with optional countdown and annotations
        and keep the last N captures in a ring buffer

    @rec <- [cap[new-recorder {history-max: 10}]]

    sync @hotkeys {
        cmd-shift-3 -> [cap[arm-and-capture @rec
                             {region: "full-screen", delay-ms: 0,
                              include-cursor: true}]]

        cmd-shift-4 -> @region <- [ui[prompt-for-rect]]
                       [cap[arm @rec
                             {region: {kind: "rect", ...@region},
                              delay-ms: 3000,
                              annotations: [
                                  {kind: "rectangle",
                                   x: 0, y: 0,
                                   width: @region:width, height: @region:height,
                                   color: "#FF0000", stroke: 2}
                              ]}]]
                       #countdown @rec

        cmd-shift-5 -> @id <- [ui[pick-window]]
                       [cap[arm-and-capture @rec
                             {region: {kind: "window", window-id: @id}}]]
    }

    at @every 100 ms
        [cap[tick {recorder: @rec, ms: 100}]]
        where @rec:state is "capturing"
        @capture <- [cap[capture {recorder: @rec,
                                    screen: [wayland[current-screen]],
                                    window-lookup: @wayland:get-window}]]
        [vault[save {path: "/screenshots/" + @capture:captured-at-ms + ".png",
                      image: @capture:image}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[cap
    new-recorder         {history-max}
    arm                  {recorder, spec}        ;; emits @armed
    arm-and-capture      {recorder, spec}        ;; convenience: arm + immediate capture if delay=0
    tick                 {recorder, ms}
    capture              {recorder, screen, window-lookup}    ;; || out-of-bounds, window-missing
    reset                {recorder}
    apply-annotations    {image, annotations}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: window lookup as injected reference

The v1 passed `window_lookup: Fn(id) -> Option<Image>` as a closure.
In Innate, a reference carries the same semantic — the resolver
decides when to call it:

[cap[capture {recorder: @rec,
               screen: [wayland[current-screen]],
               window-lookup: @wayland:get-window}]]

`@wayland:get-window` is a reference, not a value. At capture time
the resolver invokes it with the window ID.

---

## Annotations as an ordered bundle, not a pipeline

The v1 distinguished "transform pipeline" (G119) from "annotation
overlay" — same shape, different semantics. In Innate:

@annotations <- [
    {kind: "highlight", x: 0, y: 0, width: 50, height: 50,
     color: {r: 255, g: 255, b: 0}, opacity: 128}
    {kind: "rectangle", x: 10, y: 10, width: 30, height: 30,
     color: {r: 255, g: 0, b: 0}, stroke: 1}
    {kind: "arrow", x1: 5, y1: 5, x2: 45, y2: 45,
     color: {r: 0, g: 255, b: 0}}
]

`apply-annotations` folds over the list in paint order. Rectangle,
arrow, text are opaque; highlight blends via the shared alpha-blend
formula (see watermark.dpn for the canonical form).

---

## Demo

[demo
    @rec <- [cap[new-recorder {history-max: 3}]]
    [cap[arm {recorder: @rec, spec: {region: "full-screen", delay-ms: 1000}}]]
    -> @rec:state                    ;; -> "counting"
    -> @rec:countdown-remaining-ms   ;; -> 1000

    [cap[tick {recorder: @rec, ms: 400}]]
    -> @rec:countdown-remaining-ms   ;; -> 600

    [cap[tick {recorder: @rec, ms: 700}]]
    -> @rec:state                    ;; -> "capturing"

    @screen <- [img[filled {width: 10, height: 8,
                              color: {r: 100, g: 100, b: 100}}]]
    @c <- [cap[capture {recorder: @rec, screen: @screen,
                          window-lookup: @nil-lookup}]]
    -> @c:id                          ;; -> 1
    -> @c:image:width, @c:image:height   ;; -> 10, 8
]
